==English==

===Etymology===
From a later variant of {{m|en|tachy}}, {{m|en|techy}}, {{m|en|teachie}}, {{m|en|tetchy}}, simulating {{suf|en|touch|y|id2=adjectival}}. More at {{m|en|tetchy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtʌtʃi/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-touchy.ogg|Audio (US)}}
:* {{rhymes|en|ʌtʃi|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|of a situation}} Extremely [[sensitive]] or [[volatile]]; easily [[disturbed]] to the point of becoming [[unstable]]; requiring [[caution]] or [[tactfulness]].
#: ''It is an extremely '''touchy''' situation, with everybody's patience wearing thin.''
# {{lb|en|of a person}} Easily [[offended]], [[oversensitive]].
#: ''He can be very '''touchy''' when you talk about his cat, so be as tactful as possible.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|extremely sensitive}} {{l|en|touch and go}}
* {{sense|easily irritated}} {{l|en|tetchy}}, {{l|en|irritable}}, {{l|en|irascible}}, {{l|en|cranky}}

